<LegalLayout
  title="GDPR Compliance — FindThisBIN"
  description="FindThisBIN GDPR compliance — EU data residency, lawful basis, and data subject rights."
  heading="GDPR Compliance"
  lastUpdated="2026-07-01"
>
  <h2>1. Our Commitment</h2>
  <p>FindThisBIN is committed to compliance with the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). We design our engine and operations to minimize personal data exposure — the engine works exclusively with BIN prefixes and is out of the card data path by design.</p>

  <h2>2. Data Residency</h2>
  <p>For self-hosted and managed-in-your-cloud deployments, your data never leaves your VPC or chosen region. For fully-managed deployments, we offer EU-hosting with data stored in Frankfurt (eu-central-1). We do not transfer customer data outside the chosen region.</p>

  <h2>3. Lawful Basis</h2>
  <p>Processing of personal data (limited to BIN prefixes and, where applicable, contact details provided through demo/sales inquiries) is based on:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Contractual necessity</strong> — to provide the FindThisBIN engine under the service agreement</li>
    <li><strong>Legitimate interest</strong> — to respond to business inquiries and improve our services</li>
    <li><strong>Consent</strong> — where applicable (e.g., marketing communications)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Data Subject Rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR, individuals have the right to access, rectify, erase, restrict processing, object to processing, and data portability. To exercise these rights, contact <a href="mailto:privacy@findthisbin.com">privacy@findthisbin.com</a>. We respond within 30 days.</p>

  <h2>5. DPA Availability</h2>
  <p>A Data Processing Agreement is available for all customers. See our <a href={DPA_PATH}>DPA page</a> or request an executed copy at <a href="mailto:dpa@findthisbin.com">dpa@findthisbin.com</a>.</p>

  <h2>6. EU Representative</h2>
  <p>FindThisBIN's EU establishment is in Tallinn, Estonia. For GDPR-related inquiries, contact <a href="mailto:privacy@findthisbin.com">privacy@findthisbin.com</a>.</p>

  <h2>7. Supervisory Authority</h2>
  <p>You have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data protection supervisory authority. Our lead supervisory authority is the Estonian Data Protection Inspectorate (Andmekaitse Inspektsioon).</p>
</LegalLayout>
